v0.4.0 (2025-11-07)

  * Added support for Ruuvi Air by implementing the v6 format. Andreas Weiden (@graipher)

v0.3.1 (2022-06-11)

  * Improved handling of missing measurement values for Ruuvi tags. Improves
    support for Ruuvi Pro tags. Joonas Kuorilehto (@joneskoo)

  * Bluetooth UUID handling improved. UUIDs are now properly shown on output.

v0.3.0 (2022-01-27)

  * Fixed an issue where UNIX socket created by Bluewalker was not removed
    when Bluewalker exited.

  * Support for reading information advertised by Xiami Mijia sensors running
    custom firmware (https://github.com/pvvx/ATC_MiThermometer) was added by
    Ilkka Tengvall (@ikkeT)

  * Ruuvi and Mijia JSON output now include "Time" -field with timestamp when
    the advertising data was received.

  * Ruuvi and Mijia JSON ouput include "Type" -field indicating for which type
    of sensor the data is for.


v0.2.5 (2021-05-06)

 * Bluewalker can now detect if Bluetooth device does not support Bluetooth LE
   and give proper eror message to user.

 * Added timeout to HCI command execution. This ensures bluewalker does not get
   stuck waiting for response if, for whatever reason, the response never
   arrives. Currently waits 30sec for the response.

 * Decoding of manufacturer -specific data was improved, the company identifier
   is printed, if one can be resolved from the identifier in data.

 * There were minor changes to the way default, human readable, output is
   printed. No changes to JSON formats

 * Add support for running bluewalker in output mode where it creates listening
   UNIX socket (-listen-unix) and writes JSON data to all connected clients.
   In this mode the program is not terminated when clients disconnect.

 * Added Dockerfile and build.sh script which can be used to build bluewalker
   without having go installed.


v0.2.4 (2020-08-05)

 * Implement decoding for Exposure Notification Service Data used by
   Android and Apple phones to send COVID-19 Exposure Noficications.
   In collector and observer modes, the received Exposure Notification
   data is now shown decoded.

 * Add -filter-addata command line option and associated filter which can
   be used to filter devices based on the advertising data they are sending.


v0.2.3 (2020-07-13)

 * When printing advertising data in JSON format, ensure the "data" section
   contains empty array '[]' if there was no advertisment data (or none could
   be parsed).

 * Implement better support for printing debug traces. By default print only
   warning messages. This concerns mostly those using bluewalker as library,
   as there was quite a lot of debug messages being logged.


v0.2.2 (2019-08-28)

 * Add filter for showing information only about devices whose address start
   with given bytes (--filter-partial-addr 0xaabbcc or
   --filter-partial-addr aa:bb:cc)

 * When writing output to UNIX socket, terminate the program if socket is
   closed

v0.2.1 (2019-08-10)

 * Add support for file output (-output-file command line option), which
   allows to write, for example, JSON data into file in a format which is easy
   to parse.

v0.2.0 (2019-04-09)

 * Bluewalker can now read ruuvi tag data format 5 as well. The JSON output
   when listening for ruuvi tags has changed to include new fields present
   in v5 data.

 * Bluewalker now supports setting random address using -random-addr
   command line option

 * Bluewalker can be used to send advertising data. The mode is enabled with
   -broadcast command line option, advertising and scan response data can be
   set with -adv-data and -scan-resp command line options.

 * When using filters, packages matching all filters are shown instead of showing
   packets matching any filters. Filters which can have multiple values,
   like address or AD types will match any values. Hopefully this makes
   filtering a bit more intuitive.

v0.1.0 (2019-02-10)

 * Initial tagged version
